{"step_index":477,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-30T18:34:22Z","thinking":"**Adapting the Workflow**\n\nI've just created File 1. The main focus now is crafting `gta_adapted_workflow.md`. This adapts the original GTA Kids production workflow to incorporate the user's Stickman style, leveraging their implementation plan as a guide. The user's preferences for utilizing their established tools are central to this adaptation.\n\n\n**Revising Production Steps**\n\nI've significantly revised the production steps, ditching `/prompt-forge` and ElevenLabs in favor of in-game recording with Menyoo and the Rockstar Editor. I'm focusing on \"Scene & Macro Planning\" to streamline scripting, and utilizing OBS for direct screen recording to bypass rendering. This streamlines and simplifies the process significantly.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Adapted production pipeline integrating the user's proven Stickman workflow structure with the GTA 5 Kids Niche realities. Removes unnecessary steps (like scripting/voiceover) and replaces them with Menyoo recording and the compilation hack.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Execution Plan: GTA Kids Machinima Channel\n> Adapted from the proven \"Stickman Workflow\" to fit the voiceless, scriptless, 1-2 hour GTA 5 production loophole.\n\n---\n\n## What Changed From the Stickman Workflow\n| Stickman (Essay/Story) | GTA Kids (Arbitrage) |\n|---|---|\n| Deep Scripting + `/humanizer` | **Skipped.** No scripts, no humanizer. Replaced by Scene/Macro Planning. |\n| ElevenLabs Voiceover | **Skipped.** Voiceless. Replaced by Kevin MacLeod music + cartoon SFX. |\n| Nano Banana 2 Image Gen | **Skipped.** Replaced by in-game Menyoo staging + Rockstar Editor. |\n| 12-Minute Original Video | 3-5 minutes of *new* footage + 15 minutes of recycled older clips appended at the end (The \"20-Min Mid-Roll Hack\"). |\n\n---\n\n## The Sequence (ADHD-Friendly)\n\n```\nPHASE 1 (STUDY):      MARINARA / Top Competitor pattern analysis\nPHASE 2 (STABILITY):  Modding baseline setup (OpenIV, HeapAdjuster, GameConfig)\nPHASE 3 (PRODUCTION): The Daily 2-Hour Loop\n```\n\n---\n\n## Production Pipeline (Per Video — End to End)\n\n### Step 1: TOPIC & ASSET VALIDATION (30 Mins)\n→ **vidIQ:** Check trending crossover keywords (e.g., \"Spiderman vs Skibidi Toilet\").\n→ **gta5-mods.com:** Download a free Mega Ramp or Obstacle `.xml` file.\n→ **AddonPeds:** Inject the required superhero skins (free).\n→ **JulioNIB:** Verify superpower scripts are active.\n\n### Step 2: SCENE PLANNING (No Scripting) (10 Mins)\n→ Write down the 3-5 minute sequence (e.g., \"Hulk jumps off ramp in green car. Spiderman dances. Venom attacks.\")\n→ No `/prompt-forge` needed. This is pure visual dopamine planning.\n\n### Step 3: STAGING & IN-GAME RECORDING (45 Mins)\n→ Load the `.xml` map via **Menyoo Object Spooner**.\n→ Spawn peds and lock them using **Scene Director** Numpad macros.\n→ Use JulioNIB auto-combat scripts to automate fights.\n→ Press F1 to record the chaos in a single, un-cut 3-5 minute take.\n\n### Step 4: CINEMATICS & OBS CAPTURE (The Render Skip) (30 Mins)\n→ Open Rockstar Editor. Detach camera (Free Cam).\n→ Add low-angle shots, pans, and cinematic zooms to bypass the \"Reused Content\" flag.\n→ **CRITICAL:** Hide the HUD (press H) and screen-record the playback using **OBS**. Do *not* export via Rockstar Editor (takes too long).\n\n### Step 5: ASSEMBLY & SOUND DESIGN (30 Mins)\n→ Drop OBS footage into **CapCut**.\n→ **Mute all game audio** (prevents copyright/mature strikes).\n→ Add royalty-free upbeat music (Kevin MacLeod) and spam cartoon SFX (boings, whooshes) to prove \"human editorial effort\" for monetization.\n→ Append 15 minutes of your *previously uploaded* GTA videos to the end to hit the 20-minute mark.\n\n### Step 6: POLISH & PUBLISH (20 Mins)\n→ **Thumbnail:** Take a Rockstar Editor F12 screenshot. Use Photoshop. Crank vibrance to +100. Add white outer glow to the hero, red arrows, and scale the villain up 5x.\n→ **vidIQ:** Optimize title (aim for 85+ score) and copy-paste character-counted tags.\n→ Upload Long-form video. \n→ **The Bridge:** Cut the craziest 10 seconds into a Short, and use the YouTube Studio **\"Related Video\" link** to drive traffic to the long-form video.\n\n---\n\n## Tool Stack Adjustments\n\n### 1. In-Game & Assets (NEW)\n| Tool | Use |\n|------|-----|\n| OpenIV / ScriptHookV | Baseline Mod Management |\n| HeapAdjuster / GameConfig | **Mandatory** crash-prevention for heavy peds |\n| Menyoo | Set design, spawning, time/weather control |\n| Scene Director / JulioNIB | Auto-combat and animation macros |\n\n### 2. Assembly & Polish (RETAINED)\n| Tool | Use |\n|------|-----|\n| OBS (NVENC Encoder) | Screen recording (zero rendering wait) |\n| CapCut | SFX layering and 20-minute compilation stitching |\n| Photoshop | \"Deep Fry\" 200% saturation thumbnails |\n| vidIQ Web App | Titles, Tags, Keyword search |\n\n---\n\n## Daily Schedule Blocks (Adapted for GTA)\n\n| Block | Time | Hours | Use |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 🏠 Home Work | ~9-11 AM | 1-2h | vidIQ topic research, download XML maps & ped skins. |\n| 🚶 Travel | ~11-12 PM | — | To library / workspace. |\n| 📚 Deep Work | 12-6:45 PM | ~7h | Main work block. Mod debugging, Menyoo recording, OBS capture, CapCut assembly. (Expect this to take 7 hours for Video #1, dropping to 2 hours by Video #10). |\n| 🏋️ Gym (Passive) | 7-10 PM | 3h | NotebookLM audio (feed it YouTube growth strategy docs). |\n| 🟢 Light Work | 10 PM-12 AM | 1-2h | Photoshop thumbnails, final upload, schedule Shorts. |\n| 🛏️ Sleep | 12 AM | — | Hard cutoff. |\n\n---\n\n## ADHD Rules (Retained & Enforced)\n1. **Production before consumption.** No watching YouTube until your 3-5 minute OBS clip is recorded.\n2. **One thing at a time.** Don't download 50 mods at once. Download the exact 3 mods needed for today's video.\n3. **Phone in another room** during the 7-hour deep work block.\n4. **If you've been \"planning the set\" for more than 30 minutes, you're procrastinating.** Load a pre-made XML map and press record.","Description":"Workflow adaptation integrating the Stickman implementation plan with the GTA 5 Kids Niche realities.","Overwrite":false,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\efc75235-355e-455c-b598-1a3e644f6697\\gta_adapted_workflow.md","toolAction":"Adapting Stickman workflow","toolSummary":"Save adapted workflow"}}]}
